{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XLkba8tZQRrX6oHKHfFLRB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0e0255b872f08dabafe9414d623820272cd475be\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:24:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6827: Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor (#6637)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor\\n\\nFixes #6636\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Keep the outbox from enqueueing events about its own rows\\n\\nNow that onPersist reaches EventInterceptor, saving an OutboxEvent row\\npublishes a SaveDbEvent about that row. With an @OutboxEventListener\\nthat accepts it, such as one taking SaveDbEvent<?> or EntityEvent<?>,\\nOutboxEventInterceptor saved another OutboxEvent for it, and so on,\\nuntil the JVM ran out of heap on the first create or update.\\nOutboxEventInterceptor now ignores entity events whose entity is an\\nOutboxEvent.\\n\\nThe new ChainingInterceptor overrides are @since 3.0.0, because 2.9.x\\nbuilds against Hibernate 5.6, whose Interceptor has no onPersist or\\nonRemove.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Stop auditing OutboxEvent with Envers\\n\\nWith hibernate.integration.envers.enabled=true, Envers writes the audit\\nrow of each new or changed OutboxEvent just before the transaction\\ncommits, with persist(entityName, Map). The SaveDbEvent for that row has\\na HashMap as its entity, so the OutboxEvent check in\\nOutboxEventInterceptor let it through to a listener such as one taking\\nSaveDbEvent<?>. That saved another OutboxEvent, whose audit row came\\nnext, and so on, with each payload nesting the previous one. On H2 the\\ncommit ended in OutOfMemoryError. On MySQL it ended in \\\"Data too long\\nfor column 'payload'\\\", so logins and the outbox poller failed.\\n\\nOutboxEvent is no longer @Audited, as on 2.9.x.\\nEnversAuditTableInitializerDatabaseIT expected an audit table for every\\nentity with an @Audited superclass, but Envers does not audit\\nOutboxEvent through BaseOpenmrsObject's annotation, so the test now\\nchecks the entity's own annotation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"cb6cda4236b21a84cc4e1765a0dbaa58fdbe2565\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T15:17:25+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6802 Extend hasPermission to support custom rules provided from modules (#6668)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0340ada6bd4209e38630ebe7978041e0b514f85c\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T14:08:49+03:00\",\"message\":\"Initialize Context's user context holder before its logger (#6672)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6670\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7b9487cfb10a96aaad142b8fbf4f3debfa0e0105\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T13:40:41+03:00\",\"message\":\"Read the name layout global properties with a proxy privilege (#6671)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6669\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"49c3273ccd6cb49bcddbbe895f668ce0e0c4840f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T17:33:35+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6549: Logging should not be vulnerable to injection attacks (#6165)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"21ea98bdb1d1ca38a2986de62de17b8e3f7bd8a3\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T19:37:37+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6796: Fix NPE whe death date is null when merging patients (#6537)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗲𝗲𝗽\",\"authorEmail\":\"imandeepduhan@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The background job server was started while its application context was\\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\\njetty:run this logged \\\"EntityManagerFactory is closed\\\" for a job that ran\\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \\\"Task class ... not found\\\" for a\\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\\nwere loaded.\\n\\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\\n\\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b9993c839cf8ddf521e361970337c972d9729f7e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T16:07:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"Ensure core service advisors apply when modules declare FactoryBean services (#6631)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Ensure core service advisors apply when modules declare FactoryBean services\\n\\nFixes #6630\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Declare optimized proxies by their target class and test types before creation\\n\\nTransactionProxyFactoryBean definitions that set optimize get a CGLIB proxy\\nof their target from Spring, so they now declare the target class, as\\nproxyTargetClass ones do. The type-matching test now runs the post processor\\non a bare bean factory and checks the lookups before anything is created, and\\nthat they agree with the types Spring then creates, since the previous version\\nstill passed with the post processor removed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B2oUEh4gpUNZ8KRncEcwRX\\n\\n* Leave proxies whose target is a factory bean for Spring to type\\n\\nA TransactionProxyFactoryBean whose target references another factory\\nbean was declared as Object, because looking up the referenced factory\\nbean's type without creating it gives Object, so by-type lookups missed\\nthe proxy until it was created. Such definitions are now left alone, as\\ninner factory bean targets already were, and Spring determines their\\ntype as before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012oVHK8PwaoTjjKonYkfCvh\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"41c5821a9b8b2d184207c8842e4c4331e02aaa7f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T21:27:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType (#6633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType\\n\\nFixes #6632\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Document that modules map their enums with StringEnumType\\n\\nThe class Javadoc said to delete StringEnumType once Obs, ConceptName\\nand OrderSet move to annotations. Modules now map their own enums with\\nit, so say that instead.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ja9UqKCQ2eMd7FaYQ2ewqz\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b64e0729cce60c40dffb75788c4b43937a6fc77e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T08:23:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6818: Context.closeSession() closes sessions it did not open (#6651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"015b9c67043f0585d0ed6a99b46793fc46fa03a2\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T20:54:03+03:00\",\"message\":\"Restore lazy loading for associations converted from hbm mappings (#6645)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2c9b2ee0dd005f64fa543ca8228c51f57cb319c7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T10:15:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6810: Extend cluster-safety to RolePrivilegeCache (#6627)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b147e0dcae701feb4670b53a454daf0cfb210ee9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T16:07:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6684: Location.childLocations gained unintended orphanRemoval=true in the JPA migration (#6444)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Wikum Weerakutti <wikum@linuxdeveloper.space>\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f10e3fb9a645378ab6682c21d6be478bfdab6199\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T16:28:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6721: Replace StackWalker with a thread-local guard in UserDAO (#6588)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"34bd26a8166d1277f83e4fdf1bda550ff8cc49a6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T22:26:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6686: Restore relevance weighting in patient search lost in the Hibernate Search 6 migration (#6430)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a48d5d8a398069f34955affb6f783b79f122423a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T16:31:56-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6698 & TRUNK-6776: Cache @Authorized metadata and add tests for class hierarchy (#6508)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3310bc1d9682151ac461faf0916ca3da7d5a88d0\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T14:06:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Follow-up: Re-add null privilege check and add guards\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0fb13892759020f6bc0824a097518d546024eb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T13:45:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Reduce the overhead of the gzip filter (#6505)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d787a1e60899e39377ce5011b298a188b3354c6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T13:54:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6780: Add a MariaDB option to the test container harness (#6474)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit 5983a2b85e60caf1fdf7edaa8abc860d9f1dd17d)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6e77bfd03ab134fc7d66a0e3140d6e468f569ec5\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T11:39:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6697: HandlerUtil's cache should not be garbage collected (#6494)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e2056c9af9036ddef415212ec8da7b0bc2eda96e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-24T10:44:30-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6784: LoggingAdvice should have a fast exit path (#6488)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d92b490aaa25fbd255be0d08a04da4772a03e3b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-22T01:13:29+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6756: Remove deprecated Daemon thread-execution overloads (#6483)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"tejas\",\"authorEmail\":\"tejaswaghmare.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c9acac5ee18493654d161c7a99b7ae63d8134a6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T22:40:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6709: Remove internal copy amplification in Concept name resolution (#6365)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"TWIINE\",\"authorEmail\":\"122885804+Twiineenock@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d222c6085bbe13f62be68908ad9c3abbaa75db1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T12:44:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6729:  Let batch loading engage on the identifier and concept search paths (#6420)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Rohith Gurram\",\"authorEmail\":\"89861100+Rocker810@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ce847744295132bbe5fb97f369fab714f09b309\",\"date\":\"2026-08-20T19:57:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6731: Add paging support to the obs retrieval API (#6410)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cec3752e6ac0cff5f9e0cae4183db41c485ca163\",\"date\":\"2026-08-18T15:09:58-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6777: Cache the tokenization of LayoutTemplates (#6470)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"960f1cb95496e66ab8047a5f83eda6c1b2ecb2e2\",\"date\":\"2026-08-15T02:00:17+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6717: Replace reflective BeanUtils property access with direct PersonName getters (#6431)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ranidu Nethma\",\"authorEmail\":\"113999336+RaniduNethma@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"73c69ec0cea55efa51d67a8d3f19899c6eb5cf93\",\"date\":\"2026-08-14T12:44:58-07:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6758: Remove MigrationHelper (#6457)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Idontknowthough\",\"authorEmail\":\"tomlu60220244@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"05bc4e4dc32c4654aba49cc76b9252def11b06c2\",\"date\":\"2026-08-14T20:37:23+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6680: Restore lazy fetch semantics after JPA migration (#6379)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Mahesh5f4\",\"authorEmail\":\"167050186+Mahesh5f4@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8bb5c2e9e36ab8fb09f0053786bc0f040775cc1e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T20:49:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6733: Use java-uuid-generator for entity UUIDs instead of UUID.randomUUID() (#6391)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar\",\"authorEmail\":\"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"befcc055a108c28458fc21ff73f07dfe844f78a4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T10:16:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"Improve test suite run time (#6377)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"20b5abcfcfd8c73e0fbe40ea4586280bfff8f61e\",\"date\":\"2026-07-23T13:40:47+03:00\",\"message\":\"maven(deps): bump hibernateVersion from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final (#6309)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* maven(deps): bump hibernateVersion from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\\n\\nBumps `hibernateVersion` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final.\\n\\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\\n\\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-c3p0` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\\n\\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-envers` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\\n\\n---\\nupdated-dependencies:\\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core\\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\\n  dependency-type: direct:production\\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-c3p0\\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\\n  dependency-type: direct:production\\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-envers\\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\\n  dependency-type: direct:production\\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\\n...\\n\\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\\n\\n* Restore primary key on order_type_class_map join table for Hibernate 7.4\\n\\nHibernate ORM 7.4 changed set-collection DDL generation: when a Set-based\\n@ManyToMany join table declares an explicit @UniqueConstraint covering all\\nof its columns, Hibernate now emits that unique constraint in place of the\\ncomposite primary key it previously generated. OrderType.conceptClasses was\\nthe only join table carrying such a constraint, so order_type_class_map was\\ncreated without a primary key.\\n\\nNon-transactional integration tests build the schema via hbm2ddl and load\\nstandardTestDataset.xml with dbunit's REFRESH operation, which requires a\\nprimary key, so every one of them failed in setup with\\nNoPrimaryKeyException: ORDER_TYPE_CLASS_MAP.\\n\\nThe Set's composite key already enforces the exact uniqueness the annotation\\ndeclared, making uniqueConstraints redundant, and the production schema is\\ndefined by Liquibase (unaffected). Removing it restores the composite primary\\nkey and makes order_type_class_map consistent with the other @ManyToMany join\\ntables (user_role, location_tag_map, concept_name_tag_map).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dependabot[bot]\",\"authorEmail\":\"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f\",\"date\":\"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"265582974b2589ffc8787b57c2e4ba0368cb6cba\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T12:44:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Follow-up: Comment clean-up\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This was already included in the backports\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":73}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ae3967b-799a-400b-b888-5a68c6030011","uuid":"2f98ec2b-5fcc-4f74-b4a4-0cb24ff9dfc4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T05:43:29.653Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0e0255b872f08dabafe9414d623820272cd475be\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:24:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6827: Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor (#6637)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor\\n\\nFixes #6636\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Keep the outbox from enqueueing events about its own rows\\n\\nNow that onPersist reaches EventInterceptor, saving an OutboxEvent row\\npublishes a SaveDbEvent about that row. With an @OutboxEventListener\\nthat accepts it, such as one taking SaveDbEvent<?> or EntityEvent<?>,\\nOutboxEventInterceptor saved another OutboxEvent for it, and so on,\\nuntil the JVM ran out of heap on the first create or update.\\nOutboxEventInterceptor now ignores entity events whose entity is an\\nOutboxEvent.\\n\\nThe new ChainingInterceptor overrides are @since 3.0.0, because 2.9.x\\nbuilds against Hibernate 5.6, whose Interceptor has no onPersist or\\nonRemove.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Stop auditing OutboxEvent with Envers\\n\\nWith hibernate.integration.envers.enabled=true, Envers writes the audit\\nrow of each new or changed OutboxEvent just before the transaction\\ncommits, with persist(entityName, Map). The SaveDbEvent for that row has\\na HashMap as its entity, so the OutboxEvent check in\\nOutboxEventInterceptor let it through to a listener such as one taking\\nSaveDbEvent<?>. That saved another OutboxEvent, whose audit row came\\nnext, and so on, with each payload nesting the previous one. On H2 the\\ncommit ended in OutOfMemoryError. On MySQL it ended in \\\"Data too long\\nfor column 'payload'\\\", so logins and the outbox poller failed.\\n\\nOutboxEvent is no longer @Audited, as on 2.9.x.\\nEnversAuditTableInitializerDatabaseIT expected an audit table for every\\nentity with an @Audited superclass, but Envers does not audit\\nOutboxEvent through BaseOpenmrsObject's annotation, so the test now\\nchecks the entity's own annotation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"cb6cda4236b21a84cc4e1765a0dbaa58fdbe2565\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T15:17:25+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6802 Extend hasPermission to support custom rules provided from modules (#6668)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"0340ada6bd4209e38630ebe7978041e0b514f85c\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T14:08:49+03:00\",\"message\":\"Initialize Context's user context holder before its logger (#6672)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6670\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7b9487cfb10a96aaad142b8fbf4f3debfa0e0105\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T13:40:41+03:00\",\"message\":\"Read the name layout global properties with a proxy privilege (#6671)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Fixes #6669\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"49c3273ccd6cb49bcddbbe895f668ce0e0c4840f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T17:33:35+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6549: Logging should not be vulnerable to injection attacks (#6165)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"21ea98bdb1d1ca38a2986de62de17b8e3f7bd8a3\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T19:37:37+05:30\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6796: Fix NPE whe death date is null when merging patients (#6537)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗲𝗲𝗽\",\"authorEmail\":\"imandeepduhan@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The background job server was started while its application context was\\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\\njetty:run this logged \\\"EntityManagerFactory is closed\\\" for a job that ran\\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \\\"Task class ... not found\\\" for a\\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\\nwere loaded.\\n\\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\\n\\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b9993c839cf8ddf521e361970337c972d9729f7e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T16:07:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"Ensure core service advisors apply when modules declare FactoryBean services (#6631)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Ensure core service advisors apply when modules declare FactoryBean services\\n\\nFixes #6630\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Declare optimized proxies by their target class and test types before creation\\n\\nTransactionProxyFactoryBean definitions that set optimize get a CGLIB proxy\\nof their target from Spring, so they now declare the target class, as\\nproxyTargetClass ones do. The type-matching test now runs the post processor\\non a bare bean factory and checks the lookups before anything is created, and\\nthat they agree with the types Spring then creates, since the previous version\\nstill passed with the post processor removed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B2oUEh4gpUNZ8KRncEcwRX\\n\\n* Leave proxies whose target is a factory bean for Spring to type\\n\\nA TransactionProxyFactoryBean whose target references another factory\\nbean was declared as Object, because looking up the referenced factory\\nbean's type without creating it gives Object, so by-type lookups missed\\nthe proxy until it was created. Such definitions are now left alone, as\\ninner factory bean targets already were, and Spring determines their\\ntype as before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012oVHK8PwaoTjjKonYkfCvh\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"41c5821a9b8b2d184207c8842e4c4331e02aaa7f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T21:27:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType (#6633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType\\n\\nFixes #6632\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Document that modules map their enums with StringEnumType\\n\\nThe class Javadoc said to delete StringEnumType once Obs, ConceptName\\nand OrderSet move to annotations. Modules now map their own enums with\\nit, so say that instead.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ja9UqKCQ2eMd7FaYQ2ewqz\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b64e0729cce60c40dffb75788c4b43937a6fc77e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T08:23:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6818: Context.closeSession() closes sessions it did not open (#6651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"015b9c67043f0585d0ed6a99b46793fc46fa03a2\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T20:54:03+03:00\",\"message\":\"Restore lazy loading for associations converted from hbm mappings (#6645)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2c9b2ee0dd005f64fa543ca8228c51f57cb319c7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T10:15:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6810: Extend cluster-safety to RolePrivilegeCache (#6627)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b147e0dcae701feb4670b53a454daf0cfb210ee9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T16:07:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"